parts:
i’ve got the chemistry/paper/film sorted. what I need now is the box: super clear to visible, but blocks UV and/or IR.

can you:
- pull a short list of materials with spectra, typical thickness, how easy they are to cut, and rough price;
- find a few off-the-shelf clear boxes (display/card/tissue/ballot) that use those materials, with inside dims + any UV/IR notes;
- pick your best two under $100 and why;
- add a dead-simple shutter idea (slide/hinge/magnet) with a tiny BOM;
- and a quick test plan (phone IR remote + cheap UV flashlight)?
